{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"tool_calls","index":0,"message":{"content":"I have the key evidence I need. Let me work through the puzzle:\n\n**The first book:** Chigozie Obioma's *An Orchestra of Minorities* (2019) — shortlisted for the Booker Prize (the award created in the 2000s, since the Man Booker International Prize in its current form began 2005), translated into 30 languages (over 25). Obioma was born in **Akure, Nigeria** (per e1).\n\n**The prize-winning book:** Jokha Alharthi's *Celestial Bodies* — released in 2018 (Arabic original *Sayidat al-Qamar*), won the 2019 Man Booker International Prize (e2 confirms it as \"the first novel originally published in Arabic to win the Man Booker International Prize\"). The author of this prize-winning book (Alharthi) was born in the same city where Obioma grew up.\n\nThe puzzle states the prize-winning author was born in the same city where the first book's author (Obioma) grew up. Obioma was born in Akure, and Akure is where he grew up. The puzzle's logic then asks: based on this connection, in what city was the author of the first book (Obioma) born?\n\nThe answer is Akure.","role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"function":{"arguments":"{\"answer\": \"Akure\", \"refs\": [\"e1\", \"e2\"]}","name":"finish"},"id":"call_88bbea6ea59f4838a113cda3","index":0,"type":"function"}]}}],"created":1789472883,"id":"chatcmpl-de8f29e6-47eb-944f-ac5c-07fa519c2cb7","model":"glm-5.2","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"prompt_tokens":17863,"completion_tokens":296,"reasoning_tokens":0,"total_tokens":18159,"cached_tokens":0,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0},"prompt_cost":0.000000,"completion_cost":0.000000,"cache_cost":0.000000}}